# Netlify _redirects — multilingual fallbacks
#
# Per-language index pages (/es/articles/, /pt/articles/, /de/articles/) and
# /es/news/, /es/videos/ aren't built statically — only individual article
# HTML files exist under /<lang>/articles/. To prevent 404 when users click
# Crónicas/Videos/Noticias from a /<lang>/ navbar/footer, redirect those
# directory requests to the EN canonical index pages (which exist and work).
#
# This way the navbar can use locale-prefixed hrefs without 404s.
#
# Status 301 = permanent redirect; preserves SEO equity to the canonical.

/es/articles/  /articles/  301
/pt/articles/  /articles/  301
/de/articles/  /articles/  301

/es/news/  /news/  301
/pt/news/  /news/  301
/de/news/  /news/  301

/es/videos/  /videos/  301
/pt/videos/  /videos/  301
/de/videos/  /videos/  301

/es/projects/*  /projects/:splat  301
/pt/projects/*  /projects/:splat  301
/de/projects/*  /projects/:splat  301

# Article category filter URLs from translated home cards/footer also redirect
/es/articles/  /articles/  301
/pt/articles/  /articles/  301
/de/articles/  /articles/  301

# Legacy Spanish-slug privacy/terms (DetailFooter used to point there)
/privacidad  /privacy.html  301
/terminos    /terms.html    301
